Subject: [PATCH] wave: Drop obsolete BT ACS raw netlink transport

The legacy BT ACS socket reserves protocol 21, which Linux owns as
NETLINK_CRYPTO. Depending on module load order, this prevents either
mtlkroot or crypto_user from loading.

Stock hostapd ACS uses NL80211_CMD_GET_SURVEY through the existing WAVE
survey callback. Remove the unused raw transport and its interference
notification producer. Keep CCA processing, channel data reporting and
WAVE generic-netlink registration unchanged.

